 ## Honest ceiling
 
-AnonSync is still not a production peer discovery system, encrypted peer protocol, persisted transfer scheduler, file watcher, daemon, UI, invite/share-key authority, or deployable privacy-preserving distributed sync product. Rev0673 only cleans committed staged transfer sidecars after a successful local fake-session materialization. It does not persist session state, model cleanup checkpoints in SQLite, clean abandoned/in-progress transfers, run tombstone/conflict branches inside the fake session, serialize authenticated peer messages, or model peer/folder trust as non-caller-authored authority. The next durable product move is to persist manifests, apply intents, peer assignments, transfer rounds, receipts, materialization terminal states, and cleanup checkpoints.
+AnonSync is still not a production peer discovery system, encrypted peer protocol, persisted transfer scheduler, file watcher, daemon, UI, invite/share-key authority, or deployable privacy-preserving distributed sync product. Rev0674 persists a completed fake-session checkpoint only after convergence; it does not replay the checkpoint into resumed work, own abandoned transfers, persist every in-flight transfer round before crash, model tombstone/conflict branches inside the fake session, or define peer/folder trust as non-caller-authored authority. The next durable product move is to use these checkpoint rows as restart input: resume incomplete staged transfers, record cleanup terminal states before/after filesystem mutation, and promote manifest/index state into a real local sync database.
